data: {"id":"evt_0483c8977001fewcOosS7E57q0","type":"message.part.updated","properties":{"sessionID":"ses_fb7c37da5ffeGFjrpG4zR44fPU","part":{"type":"text","text":"<unpolled-background-shell-jobs>\nYou are ending your turn with 1 detached `ctx_shell` job is still outstanding:\n- `shell_1f2e3d4c5b6a7988` — `./gradlew build`\n\n`ctx_shell(run_in_background=true)` **does not notify** on completion — unlike\n`task(run_in_background=true)`, no `<system-reminder>` will ever arrive for it. If you\nend the turn expecting one, the work stalls until a human intervenes.\n\nResolve every job listed above before yielding. Pick ONE of:\n\n**A. Wait for it — bounded loop, then ONE terminal `status` call.**\nWait in a single shell call that exits as soon as the job lands:\n\n```bash\nfor i in $(seq 1 50); do\n  grep -qE \"BUILD (SUCCESSFUL|FAILED)|<your done marker>\" /tmp/job.log 2>/dev/null && break\n  sleep 2\ndone\n```\n\nThat is one call and it returns the moment the work finishes. Firing\n`background_action=\"status\"` over and over is the failure mode this replaces: it burns a\ndozen turns, floods the context, and reports nothing the loop would not have caught.\n(The \"never sleep-poll\" guidance is about a single blind `sleep 300`, which wastes the\nfull wait even when the job finished in 5s. A loop that breaks on completion is correct.)\n\n**The loop alone does NOT clear the job.** Only a `ctx_shell` call naming the job id\nderegisters it — reading a marker file, a log, or a verdict file is invisible here, so\nthis warning will fire again on work you already finished. Close every waited-on job\nwith one terminal call:\n`ctx_shell(background_action=\"status\", job_id=\"shell_1f2e3d4c5b6a7988\")`\n\n**B. You no longer need it — cancel explicitly:**\n`ctx_shell(background_action=\"cancel\", job_id=\"shell_1f2e3d4c5b6a7988\")`\n\n**C. You already consumed its result by other means.** A job whose output you read from\na file is still registered — that is the most common reason a job you know finished is\nlisted above. Same fix: one `background_action=\"status\"` call (A) clears it on a\nterminal status or `not found`; `cancel` (B) always clears it.\n\nNext time, prefer not to detach at all: `ctx_shell` runs in the FOREGROUND up to ~110s,\nwhich covers most builds and test runs. Detaching is for work that genuinely exceeds\nthat — and if the work is delegable, `task(run_in_background=true)` notifies, so it can\nbe awaited by simply ending the turn.\n</unpolled-background-shell-jobs>","messageID":"msg_0483c8973001AfYrP3Lf2e05dW","sessionID":"ses_fb7c37da5ffeGFjrpG4zR44fPU","id":"prt_0483c8973002UqYn4ioQRHf3oT"},"time":1787918322039}}

